.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-CAPTURE 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-capture \- open the OCTA-CAPTURE GTK control panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-capture\fR [\fB\-\-bin-dir\fR DIR] [\fB\-\-midi-port\fR PORT]
             [\fB\-\-data-dir\fR DIR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open the local HTML control panel inside GTK4/WebKitGTK as the regular desktop user.
The Xfce Applications menu lists it under Settings.
The panel controls preamps, compressors, direct mixers, reverb, output routing,
sample rate, Auto-Sens and preset files.
Closing it releases its CTRL connection; independent audio applications continue running.
.PP
At 192 kHz only channels 1 through 4 and Mixer A are available.
The panel reports Linux ALSA information; application/server settings own buffer size.
.PP
The default CTRL MIDI port is hw:CARD=OCTACAPTURE,DEV=0,SUBDEV=1. Close other control-panel/CTRL clients before opening it. Audio streaming is independent of this connection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-bin-dir DIR
Directory containing the C++ backend programs; installed launchers use their own binary directory.
.TP
.B \-\-midi-port PORT
Select the ALSA raw-MIDI CTRL port.
.TP
.B \-\-data-dir DIR
Private preferences and recovery directory. The default is
$XDG_STATE_HOME/octa-capture, or ~/.local/state/octa-capture.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print options without opening the device.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
